Description: VeltOS Mail, e-mail in the layout of Windows 11's new Outlook
 The blue header with the search box, the app bar (Mail, Calendar,
 People), the Home / View / Help ribbon, the folder pane with Favorites,
 the message list with Focused / Other and date groups, the reading pane,
 and new mail, reply and forward in the reading pane; "Add your account"
 on the first start. English and Turkish.
 .
 Mail is read over IMAP and sent over SMTP (Python's imaplib and smtplib,
 SSL/TLS or STARTTLS). Gmail, Yahoo, iCloud, Yandex, AOL, GMX and others
 are set up from the address alone; their mail programs need an app
 password. Outlook.com accounts need Microsoft's own sign-in (OAuth 2.0),
 which works once VeltOS Mail's client registration is configured.
 Messages are shown with JavaScript off and pictures from the internet
 blocked until the user allows them.
